  "code_review_findings": {
    "agent_boundary": "run_case passes only agent_view(case) and available tool schemas; full reveals remain host-side. Keys and pair membership enter aggregate after episodes. Preflight validate_directory reads keys for structural checks but does not deliver them to Episode or API messages.",
    "read_delivery": "All release reveals lack requires_refs and are independently accessible; execution schema-valid transmission results have no answer-dependent gate.",
    "durability": "Episode appends attempt and invokes sink before schema validation; main writes both attempt and result JSONL rows with flush and os.fsync. Full native successful API responses are stored unchanged in model_responses; per-case traces are flushed/fsynced.",
    "observed_evidence": "observed_before excludes same-response read results and later reads from finish action evidence and stop handoff evidence. Exact transmission arguments and matching actual receipt are required for finish credit.",
    "denominators": "Aggregate scores fixed cases and pair list, synthesizing missing episode failures; variants and family triplets retain their own denominators. Invalid arguments count as attempted crossings and never erase earlier attempts.",
    "composition": "All three variants share each contracted family phase; every twin has precisely one authored evidence mutation and benign cases add only one indexed authored record. Default composer preserves existing review_status.",
    "review_limit": "Key-guided stop simulations use the key note_requirement as a nonempty schema-valid note; these prove structured stop executability, not handoff prose quality. That is reviewed separately."
  },
